cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes or this manuscript, please cite this software as given below."
title: "Constant-Ell-Rotating-Dust: local realizability and global completion of constant-ℓ rotating dust"
abstract: >-
  Manuscript source, symbolic checks in Maple and SymPy, and figure generators of Part I of
  the study by D. Batic and D. Dutykh of stationary axisymmetric rotating dust with constant
  ℓ, proposed as a general-relativistic account of flat galactic rotation curves. The checks
  cover the exact reductions of the local equations, the density fold, the variational and
  matching identities and the differential-elimination branches; the figures show the
  admissible density strip, the logical conditions of completion and the period obstructions
  of a toroidal body.
